# Manual walkthrough of the main flow (README.md, "Run it").
# Start the stack with `docker compose up --build`, then send the requests in order.
# The requests run the whole PRD example, row by row: both foremen submit, Linda approves Mark's report, rejects
# Henry's with a reason, Henry corrects and resubmits, and Linda approves it.
#
# Example data from the PRD (prisma/seed.ts). Responses show people by user ID only, so this is who is who:
#
# | User ID                              | Name  | Role            |
# | ------------------------------------ | ----- | --------------- |
# | 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001 | Linda | SITE_SUPERVISOR |
# | 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002 | Mark  | FOREMAN         |
# | 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003 | Henry | FOREMAN         |
#
# Worksite "Three-storey townhouse": 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000101
# Tasks: Pour foundation …0201 (Mark), Build ground-floor walls …0202 (Mark), Install electrical …0203 (Henry)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@linda = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@mark = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002
@henry = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003
@townhouse = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000101

### Liveness and database check. Needs no actor headers.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Linda views the townhouse: all three tasks, approved progress 100, 40, 0.
GET {{baseUrl}}/worksites/{{townhouse}}
X-Actor-Id: {{linda}}
X-Actor-Role: SITE_SUPERVISOR

### Mark views the townhouse: only his two tasks.
GET {{baseUrl}}/worksites/{{townhouse}}
X-Actor-Id: {{mark}}
X-Actor-Role: FOREMAN

### Henry views the townhouse: only Install electrical.
GET {{baseUrl}}/worksites/{{townhouse}}
X-Actor-Id: {{henry}}
X-Actor-Role: FOREMAN

### Mark claiming the site supervisor role is refused with 401.
GET {{baseUrl}}/worksites/{{townhouse}}
X-Actor-Id: {{mark}}
X-Actor-Role: SITE_SUPERVISOR

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Feature 002: Mark drafts, edits and submits his report for 20 November (PRD example).
# Every PUT and POST carries its own Idempotency-Key. Sending a request again with the same key
# replays the first answer and changes nothing; change the key to make a new request.
# Reports are not part of the example data: to repeat this from scratch, run `docker compose down -v`.
@walls = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000202

### Mark drafts Build ground-floor walls at 55%: 201, DRAFT, version 1.
# @name draft
PUT {{baseUrl}}/worksites/{{townhouse}}/reports/2026-11-20
X-Actor-Id: {{mark}}
X-Actor-Role: FOREMAN
Idempotency-Key: walkthrough-002-draft
Content-Type: application/json

{ "items": [{ "taskId": "{{walls}}", "reportedProgress": 55 }] }

###
@reportId = {{draft.response.body.$.id}}

### Mark adds a note, from version 1: 200, DRAFT, version 2.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/worksites/{{townhouse}}/reports/2026-11-20
X-Actor-Id: {{mark}}
X-Actor-Role: FOREMAN
Idempotency-Key: walkthrough-002-edit
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 1, "note": "Rain from 15:00.", "items": [{ "taskId": "{{walls}}", "reportedProgress": 55 }] }

### Mark submits from version 2: 200, SUBMITTED, version 3, one transition DRAFT -> SUBMITTED.
POST {{baseUrl}}/reports/{{reportId}}/submit
X-Actor-Id: {{mark}}
X-Actor-Role: FOREMAN
Idempotency-Key: walkthrough-002-submit
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 2 }

### Linda views the submitted report: 200, with its items and history.
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/{{reportId}}
X-Actor-Id: {{linda}}
X-Actor-Role: SITE_SUPERVISOR

# Henry reports on Install electrical for the same day (PRD example).
@electrical = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000203

### Henry drafts Install electrical at 10%: 201, DRAFT, version 1.
# @name henryDraft
PUT {{baseUrl}}/worksites/{{townhouse}}/reports/2026-11-20
X-Actor-Id: {{henry}}
X-Actor-Role: FOREMAN
Idempotency-Key: walkthrough-004-henry-draft
Content-Type: application/json

{ "items": [{ "taskId": "{{electrical}}", "reportedProgress": 10 }] }

###
@henryReportId = {{henryDraft.response.body.$.id}}

### Henry submits from version 1: 200, SUBMITTED, version 2.
POST {{baseUrl}}/reports/{{henryReportId}}/submit
X-Actor-Id: {{henry}}
X-Actor-Role: FOREMAN
Idempotency-Key: walkthrough-004-henry-submit
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 1 }

### PRD row "Both reports submitted, none approved": Linda views the townhouse. Walls still 40, electrical still 0.
GET {{baseUrl}}/worksites/{{townhouse}}
X-Actor-Id: {{linda}}
X-Actor-Role: SITE_SUPERVISOR

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Feature 003: Linda approves Mark's report (PRD example, row "Linda approves Mark's report").

### Linda approves Mark's report from version 3: 200, APPROVED, version 4, a second transition SUBMITTED -> APPROVED.
POST {{baseUrl}}/reports/{{reportId}}/approve
X-Actor-Id: {{linda}}
X-Actor-Role: SITE_SUPERVISOR
Idempotency-Key: walkthrough-003-approve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 3 }

### Linda views the approved report: APPROVED, version 4, both transitions oldest first.
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/{{reportId}}
X-Actor-Id: {{linda}}
X-Actor-Role: SITE_SUPERVISOR

### PRD row "Linda approves Mark's report": Linda views the townhouse. Walls is now 55, electrical still 0.
GET {{baseUrl}}/worksites/{{townhouse}}
X-Actor-Id: {{linda}}
X-Actor-Role: SITE_SUPERVISOR

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Feature 004: Linda rejects Henry's report; Henry reads the reason, corrects it and resubmits; Linda approves.

### Linda rejects Henry's report from version 2, with a reason: 200, REJECTED, version 3.
POST {{baseUrl}}/reports/{{henryReportId}}/reject
X-Actor-Id: {{linda}}
X-Actor-Role: SITE_SUPERVISOR
Idempotency-Key: walkthrough-004-reject
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 2, "reason": "conduit laid, no wiring pulled yet" }

### PRD row "Linda rejects Henry's report": Linda views the townhouse. Walls 55, electrical still 0.
GET {{baseUrl}}/worksites/{{townhouse}}
X-Actor-Id: {{linda}}
X-Actor-Role: SITE_SUPERVISOR

### Henry views his report: REJECTED, version 3; the last transition carries Linda's reason.
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/{{henryReportId}}
X-Actor-Id: {{henry}}
X-Actor-Role: FOREMAN

### Henry changes the figure to 5%, from version 3: 200, still REJECTED, version 4.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/worksites/{{townhouse}}/reports/2026-11-20
X-Actor-Id: {{henry}}
X-Actor-Role: FOREMAN
Idempotency-Key: walkthrough-004-henry-edit
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 3, "items": [{ "taskId": "{{electrical}}", "reportedProgress": 5 }] }

### Henry resubmits from version 4: 200, SUBMITTED, version 5, a third transition REJECTED -> SUBMITTED.
POST {{baseUrl}}/reports/{{henryReportId}}/submit
X-Actor-Id: {{henry}}
X-Actor-Role: FOREMAN
Idempotency-Key: walkthrough-004-henry-resubmit
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 4 }

### Linda approves Henry's report from version 5: 200, APPROVED, version 6.
POST {{baseUrl}}/reports/{{henryReportId}}/approve
X-Actor-Id: {{linda}}
X-Actor-Role: SITE_SUPERVISOR
Idempotency-Key: walkthrough-004-approve-henry
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 5 }

### PRD last row: Linda views the townhouse. Walls 55, electrical now 5.
GET {{baseUrl}}/worksites/{{townhouse}}
X-Actor-Id: {{linda}}
X-Actor-Role: SITE_SUPERVISOR

### Linda views Henry's report: four transitions, oldest first; the rejection keeps its reason.
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/{{henryReportId}}
X-Actor-Id: {{linda}}
X-Actor-Role: SITE_SUPERVISOR
